  "structure": {
    "block_count": 68,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Everything to Know About Your 6-Month-Old’s Sleep Schedule",
        "text_sha256": "2389bc6a62e8b54bf5b459939d7de239e9780f5efaafdc0129e64be8983cd37c",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "6-month-old's sleep schedule",
        "text_sha256": "f7ced7a1c7a36a30d808ddb3a3558ee22128dd64e5c1a8a0cd832e63b9842dd1",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your baby's snooze patterns are changing like crazy these days. Here's how to help your 6-month-old sleep better at the half-year mark.",
        "text_sha256": "9e8ea04197ee0773a379d3aca364990d1585d264a82ee9b7fe740072e4dc67c9",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "By the 6-month mark, your baby is — let's be honest — off-the-charts cute and clever. Her focus is turning outward, and she engages everyone around her with eye contact, gummy smiles, non-stop giggles, and lots of delightful babbling.",
        "text_sha256": "59d10775930a42620151e78d165e5af92e3315b6d70b32b9f585a3d9f848b0e4",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Held upright, your child can now practice standing and doing mini-squats. During playtime, she may have swapped plushies and toe pulling for toys and games that support her rapidly developing motor skills. Her teeth are starting to come in, if they haven't already, and her appetite is kicking into high gear. You may have added solid food (portions of pureed fruits, vegetables, and cereal) to her usual diet of breast milk or formula.",
        "text_sha256": "5254e9a7756b0c8c069fbc35ca839cb9352c4d67d6c5d68c7bb26f6cae7ac3ec",
        "word_count": 73
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As her personality develops, so do her sleep habits. She may still be a cat napper, power sleeper, night owl, or morning glory, but her sleep needs are changing. Here's what you need to know about your 6-month-old's sleep patterns.",
        "text_sha256": "f1361196fe83101a23d3a8cf745d1fe749c5d2aa5a6a70b2501d38a2157784e4",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Your 6-month-old will need at least 15 hours of sleep per day, including two to three naps and nine to 11 hours at night. Some little ones may drop from three naps to two around this age, though sleep patterns can still be unpredictable.",
        "text_sha256": "bfd7ea4ffa726156edbf30c09f0961779d8417510826075ec041781557ceefac",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Developmental milestones, teething, and the 6-month sleep regression can cause night waking, early rising, or fussiness. Keeping a consistent bedtime routine and maintaining age-appropriate naps can help improve her rest.",
        "text_sha256": "17ac1400e2070383563ba1817930532dba664ec065a0e82dccd484a65157ffa1",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "At this age, babies can begin learning self-soothing. Sleep training methods such as Ferber can work for some families. Staying active during the day and maintaining a calming pre-sleep routine also support better sleep.",
        "text_sha256": "0e95f78c20b76d638b73cacd78cfea9ce5a3b0cc79e86d536aa185eafabee2be",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How much should a 6-month-old sleep?",
        "text_sha256": "8c48024eb884fd58f96bdab0707cca255ebb2b388edef86aa7722442327bd84d",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your 6-month-old should sleep about 15 hours a day, fitting in two or three naps in addition to the nine to 11 hours of sleep she's logging at night.",
        "text_sha256": "314cf85d065077759639a0fa18861a0b798b7f9175e9df7495963edaa703f1bc",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If she dozes like a dream, sticks to a schedule and all is calm in your household, congratulations. It's also perfectly normal if your 6-month-old's routine continues to be a little unpredictable, especially because another sleep regression can rear its head this month.",
        "text_sha256": "7255a209e3b48b86ac5c6d195755ecb82242c4215f5b49704ac9ad66200c39c4",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Some babies naturally transition from topsy-turvy newborn sleep patterns into a regular schedule. But it's not uncommon for her half-year sleep routine to resemble an abstract painting: a thing of beauty to her, but baffling to everyone else.",
        "text_sha256": "2257c70c57372b48e236e7133660acdb73b70e1e45d9036188bf3fed374364ea",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If she's often cranky, finicky at meals, or showing other signs of mild sleep deprivation — all quite common for this milestone, particularly if she's going through the 6-month sleep regression — know that you're not alone, and there are a few steps you can take to improve her sleep.",
        "text_sha256": "87871ca7cd01c92002c83f547d1ae52ac43d4d4a54c9677eb4cf6ba0611c7896",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Sample sleep schedule for a 6-month-old",
        "text_sha256": "567702d8715b25220c861a3e73e33c5073ecd3d0e388b67dfff627a704177f99",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "What's the best schedule for your 6-month-old baby? While there's no one-size-fits all sleep routine , your child may be in the process of dropping a nap around the half-year mark. Depending on whether she's taking three or two naps, here are sample schedules you can adapt to her preferences.",
        "text_sha256": "a5822e54a93e0a58345b7672124ea04282a0e9f1ac49864f78fe1968d2110f0e",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
